// ==============================================================================
// DISTILL — Omni-Mind consolidation: summarize a memory into a general one
// (v0.1 STUB)
// ==============================================================================
//
// distill(id) takes a memory and returns a more general memory that
// captures what it has in common with its neighbours, so the graph stays
// small and the knowledge stays reusable. The full version does this by
// anti-unification (extract the shared AST skeleton across episodic
// traces) plus an MDL check (promote only when the distillation shrinks
// the total graph size while passing all historical regression fixtures).
//
// v0.1 is a stub: it returns the memory unchanged. The distillation
// algorithm (anti-unification + MDL) is a later phase, once the graph is
// large enough for consolidation to matter and the proposer loop exists
// to search for shared skeletons.
//
//   distill(id) -> id (identity; the memory is unchanged in the stub)
//
// Note: this file does not include std/ itself. The including file
// includes std/math.omni and std/trit.omni first if it needs them.
// ==============================================================================

#[strict]
#[cap(AI)]
#[step_budget(24000)]
#[mem_budget(8192)]
fn distill(id: i64) -> i64 {
    // STUB: return the memory unchanged. Full distillation (anti-unification
    // + MDL) comes later. The signature is the contract: a distilled
    // memory id comes back, so callers can already be written against it.
    return id;
}
